		{"id":"4aed4d4740dfba9a","type":"text","text":"Underneath seemingly obvious questions like \"who owns this\" are more fundamental questions about sovereignty, power, and politics.\n\n**Question: what is property's relationship to the state?** \n- Sovereign state (Royal Proclamation; Wildlife Act)\n- Int'll legal order (Henderson; Peace and Friendship treaties)\n- Precedes the state (Locke; Pierson)\n- Norms (Harrison v Carswell; Pierson v Post)\n\n\n\n**Question: what is property's relationship to the market (capitalism)?**\n- property as efficient \n\n**Question: what is property's relationship to society?**\n- constitutive political economy\n- historial materialism","x":-193,"y":-1360,"width":335,"height":580},
		{"id":"19d5b98287d338e2","type":"text","text":"Property and Sovereignty","x":280,"y":-763,"width":250,"height":60},
